  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will learn how to explain the difference between an arithmetic and a geometric sequence. You will determine arithmetic sequences that will help you solve real-world problems, such as how much fuel is left in your vehicle or how fast the money in your bank account is increasing.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    Explain what it means for a sequence to be arithmetic or geometric.
  </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the<emphasis> activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    4.16.1: Interpreting Function Notation
  </item>
  <item>
    4.16.2: What Is an Arithmetic Sequence?
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      4.16.2: Self Check
    </item>
    <item>
      4.16.2: Additional Resources
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.16.3: A Sequence Is a Type of Function
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      4.16.3: Self Check
    </item>
    <item>
      4.16.3: Additional Resources
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.16.4: Identify and Generate Sequences
  </item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item>
    4.16.5: Practice
  </item>
  <item>
    4.16.6: Lesson Summary
  </item>
</list></section>
